<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef uneven on moderate demand and offerings. Select and Choice rib and round cuts generally steady, while the chuck and loin cuts are higher, especially in the Select cuts. Beef trimmings steady on light demand and offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>-------</p>
<p>166 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 14 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>36 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     105.84	105.79	100.13	 99.63</p>
<p>Changes	   0.41	  0.06	  1.17	  0.83</p>
<p>Rib	  160.98	160.48	149.15	149.78</p>
<p>Chuck	 72.67	 70.98	 74.32	 70.56</p>
<p>Round	 89.48	 89.48	 86.66	 86.66</p>
<p>Loin	 173.99	176.41	153.81	156.37</p>
<p>Brisket     56.99	 56.99	 57.08	 57.08</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  66.50	 66.42	 66.75	 66.57</p>
<p>Flank	 58.29	 58.29	 58.03	 58.03</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
